[{:db/id "q-156192/selection/deab861fcde4d97e9620244ec09585293d4d0f38baacfa330084efaf15fc5cfc" :answer/id #uuid "d92be062-f23a-5ae3-9bab-6ce2dec4818c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156192/selection/a5839b1e7c6d07232ae6f92a26fc3d7c628a71925b32d11fb1f159b763e5536f" :answer/id #uuid "7791ebe8-5281-5de1-931d-24d8361211ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156192/selection/2975a59a267852917cc6f11a023dfb0a3a74e161efa53fb66f82b5f65ecee9d0" :answer/id #uuid "7c97e840-f296-503d-88e5-9cf4fc8a4408" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156192/selection/7f0f2478ce521aa4000523fe155bfe972c7a8cc195da49dd5eb0249ef8194675" :answer/id #uuid "404a9778-2b59-5121-8fbb-9423bf284569" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156192/selection/8eb9e3bf1860d90d4d5da1878dcdab2c2ce316bc13d6c4c5c0bbaacaff112984" :answer/id #uuid "652acd58-20e1-5135-b4af-84b85fa6aabd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156192/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab8e5837-811c-5c91-a54d-f7aaf6cfb9ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-156192/selection/8eb9e3bf1860d90d4d5da1878dcdab2c2ce316bc13d6c4c5c0bbaacaff112984" :answer-field/choices ["q-156192/selection/deab861fcde4d97e9620244ec09585293d4d0f38baacfa330084efaf15fc5cfc" "q-156192/selection/a5839b1e7c6d07232ae6f92a26fc3d7c628a71925b32d11fb1f159b763e5536f" "q-156192/selection/2975a59a267852917cc6f11a023dfb0a3a74e161efa53fb66f82b5f65ecee9d0" "q-156192/selection/7f0f2478ce521aa4000523fe155bfe972c7a8cc195da49dd5eb0249ef8194675" "q-156192/selection/8eb9e3bf1860d90d4d5da1878dcdab2c2ce316bc13d6c4c5c0bbaacaff112984"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-156192" :question/id #uuid "456bde2b-ef1e-54aa-8da0-4de187218c6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-156192" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{8}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=A,$ what is the value of ${\\int }_{-8}^{0}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡((-x)^{3}) \\\\  & =(-x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3}) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-8}^{8}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the adjacent intervals rule for integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-8}^{8}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-8}^{0}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{8}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-8}^{0}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+A & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-8}^{0}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =-A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-156192/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebbaf66e-6155-510f-b4d8-e38dd4c4f05c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-156192"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316128/field-1/b0abf4f3840775218c55d4f317cb0c7770b27344c26735c40c11cc36b8f330c2" :answer/id #uuid "4be6f67a-d2ec-5bc9-a9cd-458f72abdb7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-p" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316128/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c041021-1d80-557e-893e-8b852062da80" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316128/field-1/b0abf4f3840775218c55d4f317cb0c7770b27344c26735c40c11cc36b8f330c2" :answer-field/choices ["q-316128/field-1/b0abf4f3840775218c55d4f317cb0c7770b27344c26735c40c11cc36b8f330c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316128" :question/id #uuid "ad0b6114-b30d-54df-8d07-1628e7d83ec4" :question/math-academy-id "q-316128" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{4}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=p,$ express the value of ${\\int }_{-4}^{0}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x$ in terms of $p.$\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{0}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x),$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x).$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x){e}^{(-x)^{2}+1} \\\\  & =-x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{4}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the adjacent intervals rule for integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-4}^{0}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{4}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-4}^{0}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x+p & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-4}^{0}x{e}^{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =-p.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-316128/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebbaf66e-6155-510f-b4d8-e38dd4c4f05c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316128"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
